      "writtenOn": "2021-07-02T22:45:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could do that, but I am not sure by itself how it would prevent the crash caused by calling nri.unlinkDeathRecipient() twice for the same NRI?\n\nWould it work if we do what you suggest and add a check right before l.4199 to return if there was no requests? E.g.,\n\n    if (nri.mRequests.isEmpty()) {\n        logwtf(\"some error message here since this shouldn\u0027t happen\");\n        return;\n    }\n\nThis way we don\u0027t call nri.unlinkDeathRecipient() twice and essentially have a no-op. This was more or less what I intended with the checked boolean previously which was only true if mNetworkRequests.remove on l.4191 wasn\u0027t null.\n\nI also included a wtf log above to give us visibility into potential issues with our nri management. Let me know if you\u0027d rather I not.",
      "parentUuid": "3dfa6c92_dc50b418",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4240,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 4240,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "ac5b3139d5304bc83e71fe9e6b579605ac57e294",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
